QuestGuidance.Register("en",26,{
[801]="70042FF3\n1\tDefeat snow-beasts in the Misty Mountains (total: 8)\030Defeat snow-lurkers in the Misty Mountains (total: 4)\tSnow-beasts and snow-lurkers can be found throughout the Misty Mountains. Bingo is worried that his adventure will lull future readers to sleep, and wants to add some spice to his journey.\n2\tTalk to Bingo at Glóin's camp\tBingo has decided to stop for a short rest at Glóin's camp, in the Misty Mountains, near the southward road to Rivendell.\n3\tTravel north of Glóin's camp, toward the Northern Bruinen Source area of the Misty Mountains\tBingo wants to travel north of Glóin's camp into the Northern Bruinen Source area of the Misty Mountains, in an effort to add some excitement to his journey.\n4\tTalk to the injured dwarf in the narrow pass\tYou have encountered an injured dwarf in the narrow pass between the western and northern Bruinen source regions of the Misty Mountains, and should do what you can to help him.\n5\tTalk to Bingo in the narrow pass\tBingo is in the narrow pass north of Glóin's camp, worrying about the wounds of the injured dwarf you encountered.\n6\tBingo has asked you to search the Bruinen Source areas for clumps of herbs that may help heal the injured dwarf you encountered. He said you should watch Willem Whisker's reactions as you examine such herbs to determine if they will be helpful or hurtful.\t\n7\tApply the handful of healing herbs to the injured dwarf\tBingo is in the narrow pass north of Glóin's camp, worrying about the wounds of the injured dwarf you encountered. You have a handful of (possibly) healing herbs, and should bring them to the injured dwarf.\n8\tTalk to Bingo in the narrow pass\tBingo is in the narrow pass north of Glóin's camp, worrying about the wounds of the injured dwarf you encountered.\n",
[802]="70065668\n1\tHunt boars for fresh meat (total: 8)\tAsórkho has asked you to hunt some more boars for fresh meat. You can find boars in the boar wallow north-east of Halach.\n2\tTalk to Asórkho\tYou have obtained a good amount of fresh boar meat. You should return and talk to Asórkho near the boar wallow.\n3\tTalk to Irodon in Halach\tAsórkho has given you preserved meat to give to the townsfolk of Halach, and asked you to keep his identity a secret. You should return to Irodon in Halach.\n",
[803]="7004A3A2\n1\tMulnír has asked you to speak to gather the men around the Foothold in Udûn, and tell them where to meet.\t\n2\tMulnír has asked you to collect what personal belongings of Captain Lachír you could find around the Foothold camp in Udûn.\t\n3\tMeet across the road\tYou should meet Mulnír and the other men up on the high platform across the road from the Udûn Foothold.\n4\tTalk to Mulnír\tYou should talk to Mulnír on the platform where the men have gathered to mourn Captain Lachír, across the road from the Foothold in Udûn.\n5\tLay Lachír's belongings down\tThe mourners are gathered on the high platform across the road from the Udûn Foothold. You should lay the Captain's belongings in the middle of the circle of mourners.\n6\tListen to Barathron\tThe mourners are gathered on the high platform across the road from the Udûn Foothold. Listen to Barathron speak.\n7\tTalk to Coldan\tThe mourners are gathered on the high platform across the road from the Udûn Foothold. Hear Coldan's memory of Lachír.\n8\tMourn with the others\tThe mourners are gathered on the high platform across the road from the Udûn Foothold. You should mourn with the others.\n9\tTalk to Othras\tThe mourners are gathered on the high platform across the road from the Udûn Foothold. Hear Othras' memory of Lachír.\n10\tTalk to Mulnír\tThe mourners are gathered on the high platform across the road from the Udûn Foothold. You should talk to Mulnír again.\n11\tReturn to the Foothold\tYou should return to the Foothold in Udûn now that the gathering to remember Lachír is over.\n12\tTalk to Mulnír\tYou should talk to Mulnír in the Foothold camp in Udûn.\n",
[804]="7005293E\n1\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should listen around the waters of Laerlad for the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n2\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should notate the parchment with the music that you have heard of the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n3\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should listen around the waters of Laerlad for the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n4\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should notate the parchment with the music that you have heard of the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n5\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should listen around the waters of Laerlad for the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n6\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should notate the parchment with the music that you have heard of the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n7\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should listen around the waters of Laerlad for the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n8\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should notate the parchment with the music that you have heard of the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n9\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should listen around the waters of Laerlad for the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n10\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should notate the parchment with the music that you have heard of the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n11\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should listen around the waters of Laerlad for the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n12\tTauralindalë may be hiding in and around the waters of Laerlad. You should notate the parchment with the music that you have heard of the song of Tauralindalë.\t\n13\tBring the song to Radagast and sing it for him\tRadagast can be found at Rhosgobel. You should bring the song to Radagast.\n14\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast can be found at Rhosgobel. You should talk to Radagast.\n15\tExamine the waters around Rhosgobel (total: 2)\tWaters can be found at Rhosgobel. You should examine the waters to see if anything has changed.\n16\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast can be found at Rhosgobel. You should talk to Radagast.\n",
[805]="70000073\n1\tTalk to Piper Prescott\tPiper Prescott, a renowned minstrel, is often within the common room of The Prancing Pony, in the town of Bree. You have been told to seek the teaching of Piper Prescott, an adventuring minstrel of great ability.\n2\tHelp Leland Underhill\tLeland Underhill is probably at the West Gate of the town of Bree, about to set out for the hideout of some brigands. Piper Prescott, a renowned minstrel, has asked you to help Leland Underhill and compose a song about your experience to sing in the common room of The Prancing Pony.\n3\tTalk to Piper Prescott\tPiper Prescott is in the common room of The Prancing Pony, in the town of Bree. Now that you have helped Leland Underhill, Piper Prescott will want to hear the tale.\n4\tJump onto a table near Piper Prescott and sing the Tale of Leland's Lunch\tThe tables near Piper Prescott would be ideal places to sing your song. Piper Prescott has told you to jump onto one of the tables near him and to sing your song for the company.\n5\tJump onto a table near Piper Prescott and sing the Tale of Leland's Lunch\tThe people gathered in The Prancing Pony wait to give judgement on your performance of the \"Tale of Leland's Lunch.' You have sung your tale and await judgement.\n6\tTalk to Piper Prescott\tPiper Prescott is in the common room of The Prancing Pony. Piper Prescott is waiting to give his judgement on the performance of your song.\n",
[806]="700544B7\n1\tEnter the Song-house of Lindalírë\tGirithos can be found in the Song-house of Lindalírë. You should defeat Girithos and those that serve him.\n2\tDefeat foes in the Song-house of Lindalírë (total: 6)\030Defeat Girithos\tGirithos can be found in the Song-house of Lindalírë. You should defeat Girithos and those that serve him.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated Girithos and those that serve him.\n",
[807]="7006F2F6\n1\tMeet with Rahâzi on the road to Lâkindar in An Shêru\tRahâzi asked to meet you on the road to Lâkindar, in south-west An Shêru.\n2\tTalk to Rahâzi on the road to Lâkindar\tRahâzi watches the road south toward Lâkindar.\n3\tScout what has become of Lâkindar today\tThe mines once known as Lâkindar are in south-west An Shêru.\n4\tDefeat wights and shades at Lâkindar (total: 8)\tThe wights and shades of Lâkindar should be defeated in memory of Shurug-nîn.\n5\tTalk to Rahâzi on the road to Lâkindar\tRahâzi watches the road south toward Lâkindar.\n6\tTalk to Glorfindel at Khanâg Gur, north of Damudûr\tGlorfindel is likely at Khanâg Gur, north of Damudûr.\n7\tTalk to Rahâzi at Khanâg Gur\tRahâzi is at Khanâg Gur.\n8\tTalk to Glorfindel at Khanâg Gur\tGlorfindel is at Khanâg Gur.\n9\tTalk to Rahâzi at Khanâg Gur\tRahâzi is at Khanâg Gur.\n",
[808]="70017926\n1\tTalk to Andrew Oakhurst\tAndrew Oakhurst is by the West-gate of Bree. You have been told to speak to Andrew Oakhurst about participating in the spear-training that he often runs for Wardens in Bree-land.\n2\tTalk to Andrew Oakhurst and join his line of Wardens\tAndrew Oakhurst is at the West-gate of the town of Bree. A band of brigands march on Bree from the south, and Andrew Oakhurst has asked you to join his line of Wardens in repelling them.\n3\tTalk to Andrew Oakhurst\tAndrew Oakhurst is at the West-gate of Bree. You have stood in the line that defended Bree from attack and should speak now with Warden Oakhurst.\n",
[809]="7001CC65\n1\tDefeat Ulkúrzlam at Durbúrz-stazg\tDurbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion. Aemeldir has asked you to defeat the Black Uruk Ulkúrzlam at Durbúrz-stazg. You will need to enter the encampment through the eastern gate.\n2\tTalk to Aemeldir at Echad Sirion\tEchad Sirion lies to the south of Durbúrz-stazg. You should return to Aemeldir with news of your victory against Ulkúrzlam and his soldiers.\n",
[810]="70054804\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern blade\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Forge a guild-pattern blade.\n2\tTalk to Cottar Tunnelly\030Turn in a guild-pattern blade (quantity: see journal) to Cottar Tunnelly\030Talk to the Weaponsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern blade (quantity: see journal) to the Weaponsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[811]="70054803\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern crossguard\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Forge a guild-pattern crossguard.\n2\tTalk to Cottar Tunnelly\030Turn in a guild-pattern crossguard (quantity: see journal) to Cottar Tunnelly\030Talk to the Weaponsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern crossguard (quantity: see journal) to the Weaponsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[812]="70054802\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern pommel\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Make a guild-pattern pommel.\n2\tTalk to Cottar Tunnelly\030Turn in a guild-pattern pommel (quantity: see journal) to Cottar Tunnelly\030Talk to the Weaponsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern pommel (quantity: see journal) to the Weaponsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[813]="70054801\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern scabbard\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Craft a guild-pattern scabbard.\n2\tTalk to Cottar Tunnelly\030Turn in a guild-pattern scabbard (quantity: see journal) to Cottar Tunnelly\030Talk to the Weaponsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern scabbard (quantity: see journal) to the Weaponsmith's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[814]="70019009\n1\tEnter the maze\tThe entrance to the hedge maze is near the festival grounds in the Horse-fields, a distance to the north of Bree-town. Gil Plover has challenged you to get through the maze, from start to finish, before the time runs out. The time he has allotted is three minutes.\n2\tFind your way out before the time expires\tThe exit to the hedge-maze is around here somewhere...or is it? You should try to find your way out of the maze before the time runs out. Gil Plover got out in no time at all compared to the amount you've been given. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Gil Plover outside the maze in the Horse-fields\tGil Plover is standing near the hedge maze, which is very near the festival grounds of Bree-land, north of Bree-town. You should speak with Gil Plover, for you can prove that you were able to best his challenge that you would not get through the maze in admirable time.\n",
[815]="7004C12E\n1\tParticipate in Harvest Festival activities (total: 10)\tEvery day there is something to do during the Harvest Festival. Come and join everyone at the Party Tree, Wistmead, and housing neighbourhoods and participate in many Harvest Festival activities!\n2\tRosa can be found by the Party Tree and in Wistmead. Rosa Hornblower would like to thank you for your participation in the Harvest Festival today.\t\n",
[816]="700350F3\n1\tDefeat Balewood hewers (total: 6)\tBalewood hewers can be found to the north-west of Núrzum's Wrath in central Balewood. Húna and the others have supported your choice to seek out the Orc-hewers mentioned in Lomor's missive. The note mentioned they were stationed off the roadway near where Lomor was felled, so there you can begin your search for the trees that attacked the Orcs.\n2\tSearch the hewn glade for signs of Huorns or Ents\tThe hewn glade stretches away from the roadway in central Balewood. You have slain the hewers of which the note spoke, but there remains no sign of the moving trees it also mentioned. You should search the hewn glade and see if any Orcs have found such things.\n3\tExamine the fallen Ent and Orcs more closely\tThe fallen Ent and Orcs can be found in the middle of the hewn glade in central Balewood. You have encountered the aftermath of a grim battle that occurred recently. You should examine the scene more closely to better understand what has happened.\n4\tExamine the slain Orc\tThe slain Orc is lying on the ground near the felled Ent. A slain Orc appears to have been making a run for its life before the Ent dealt its final blow. You should examine the Orc in hopes of better understanding what has occurred here.\n5\tFind and talk to the Ents in northern Balewood\tThe Ents can likely be found to the north-east of the hewn glade based on the trail of Orcs. Other Ents appear to have escaped the grim scene you stumbled upon and travelled to the north. You should find and aid them before any other Orcs can discover their location.\n",
[817]="700375BB\n1\tTalk to Winegar\tWinegar is at the inn in Stoke. Thane Ordlac informed you that Winegar, Reeve Fríthild's physician, asked to speak with you privately.\n2\tTalk to Alfbert\tAlfbert is at the inn in Stoke. Perhaps Alfbert saw the stranger Winegar mentioned. You should speak with him.\n3\tFind Grimlac\tThe stranger, Grimlac, was seen headed out the north-east gate of Stoke on horseback. Alfbert directed you to follow after Grimlac.\n4\tSearch Grimlac's body\tYou should search Grimlac's body for evidence of foul play to bring to Thane Ordlac.\n5\tBring the poison to Thane Ordlac\tThane Ordlac is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should bring the poison you found to Thane Ordlac.\n",
[818]="70067161\n1\tCheck the highest crate used in The Stacking Game for rock-scrapers\tSomeone needs to check the highest crate used in The Stacking Game for the rock-scrapers demanded by Shegai.\n2\tBring the rock-scrapers to Yared\tYared is waiting for you to descend and speak to him.\n3\tBring the rock-scrapers to Shegai\tShegai is in the Armoury of Furukzahar.\n",
[819]="7002FD3C\n1\tBurn half-orc banners (total: 8)\tThe half-orc camp can be found to the north-east of Garsfeld. Gísil wants you to assault the half-orc camp and burn their banners.\n2\tTalk to Gísil at the Mead Hall of Garsfeld\tGísil can be found inside the Mead Hall of Garsfeld, south-west of the half-orc camp. You should return to Gísil with news of your success.\n",
[820]="7000EA99\n1\tDefeat Blökk\tBlökk can be found on the west shore of the lake. Mirja has asked you to slay the Warg Blökk in an effort to protect Kauppa-kohta.\n2\tTalk to Mirja\tMirja is at Kauppa-kohta. With Blökk defeated, you should return to Mirja with news of your victory.\n",
[821]="7001759A\n1\tFind the missing text\tHorngaz is somewhere within the Foundations of Stone. Celofa has asked you to acquire the missing text from the Orc Horngaz.\n2\tReturn to Celofa\tCelofa is in the Foundations of Stone. You should return to Celofa with the scroll.\n",
[822]="700613DA\n1\tAdamanda North-took has everything she needs for her Grand Plan!\t\n2\tSpeak to Adamanda\tAdamanda is in Yondershire. You should speak with Adamanda North-took.\n",
[823]="7004CE8C\n1\tCollect a Dale coin from the banker\030Collect Snakewood from a trader\030Collect a dwarf-made puzzle box\tA coin can be collected from the banker in the Dale Crafting Hall, the wood from a foreign trader in the lower markets near the eastern gate, and the puzzle-box from a dwarf craftsman in Dale's upper markets, in the centre of town. Collect a gold coin of Dale, some Ilon-ôtin, or Snakewood, and a dwarf-made puzzle box for Queen Regent Erna.\n2\tReturn to Erna\tYou should return to Queen Regent Erna with the items she asked you to gather, inside the Great-keep in Dale.\n3\tPresent the puzzle-box\tThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale. You should present Bryn and Erna with the puzzle box.\n4\tHear Erna's remonstrance\tThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale. Hear more from Queen Regent Erna.\n5\tPresent the Snakewood\tThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale. You should present Bryn and Erna with the Snakewood.\n6\tHear Erna's remonstrance\tThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale. Hear more from Queen Regent Erna.\n7\tPresent the coin of Dale\tThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale. You should present Bryn and Erna with the coin of Dale.\n8\tHear Erna's remonstrance\tThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale. Hear more from Queen Regent Erna.\n9\tHear Bryn speak\tThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale. Bryn has grown tired of listening and speaks out of turn.\n10\tTalk to King Bard II\030Talk to Queen Regent Erna\tThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale. Bryn has grown tired of listening and speaks out of turn.\n",
[824]="7003FC05\n1\tTalk to Rosfin atop Morlad\tLady Rosfin can be found outside her home atop Morlad in Blackroot Vale. Steward Malthellam has asked you to speak to Lady Rosfin on his behalf and persuade her to aid him as an advisor.\n2\tCollect Lord Duinhir's notes\tLord Duinhir's notes can be found inside his and Lady Rosfin's home atop Morlad in Blackroot Vale. Lady Rosfin rejected Malthellam's offer based on his recent failure to protect Tingobel. She offered Lord Duinhir's notes and nothing more.\n3\tDeliver Lord Duinhir's notes to Malthellam\tMalthellam can be found near the entrance of Morlad in north-western Blackroot Vale. You have spoken to Lady Rosfin, who rebuffed Malthellam's request. She offered only Lord Duinhir's notes, which you should bring to Malthellam.\n",
[825]="7006753E\n1\tCollect spider-webs at Maj Khibi (total: 8)\tSpider-webs can be found at Maj Khibi, north-west of Kafagur.\n2\tTalk to Kúlthrak at Kafagur\tYou've collected enough spider-webs. You should bring them back to Kúlthrak at Kafagur.\n",
[826]="70071602\n1\tDefeat bees in Medân Makhai (total: 10)\030Harvest honeycombs (total: 8)\tSênjar, a local farmer in Sormedân, has requested your help in the harvest of honey from the local bees. These bees have become much more violent and aggressive since a new queen established herself over their hive. The bees can be found within the cave of Medân Makhai, north-west of Sormedân.\n2\tReturn to Sênjar in Sormedân with the recovered honey\tReturn to Sênjar in Sormedân with the recovered honey.\n",
[827]="7001567D\n1\tDefeat Orcs at Skrithûrz-ulíma (total: 10)\tThe White-hand Orcs of Khazad-dûm can be found in great number in Skrithûrz-ulíma, near the centre of Zelem-melek. The time has come to strike a critical blow against Moria's Orcs.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have devastated the presence of Orcs in Skrithûrz-ulíma, making one small pocket of Zelem-melek less treacherous for the vulnerable expedition.\n",
[828]="70037794\n1\tDefeat Dunlending stone-carriers (total: 15)\tKeep the three Rohirrim archers protected and coordinate their firing against the Dunlending stone carriers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[829]="7003A4A4\n1\tDefeat Dunlending stone carriers (total: 20)\tDunlending men have begun carrying loose stones towards the Dike in an attempt to dam the stream through the trench. The Rohirrim archers will do what they can to prevent the barrier from being erected, but will need your leadership to coordinate their fire. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[830]="7005293B\n1\tGather field stones (total: 10)\tField stones can be found near the edge of the woods in Laerlad. You should gather field stones for Evorik.\n2\tPlace field stones next to the crumbling wall in Blómgard (total: 2)\tCrumbling walls can be found in Blómgard. You should place the stones next to the crumbling walls in Blómgard so the Woodfolk may repair them.\n3\tTalk to Evorik\tEvorik can be found in Blómgard. You should talk to Evorik.\n",
[831]="70020DBB\n1\tDefeat Enaid-helgi at night\tEnaid-helgi appears at night upon a plateau to the north-east of Rhus Cornchúthur. Rhus Cornchúthur suggested that the mayor of his people might speak with you if you were to prove yourself to him. Slaying the demon-dog Enaid-helgi would go a long way towards that goal.\n2\tTalk to Rhus Cornchúthur in the Gloomglens\tRhus Cornchúthur awaits your return south-west of Enaid-helgi's hunting ground. You should return to Rhus Cornchúthur with news of your victory.\n",
[832]="700378F5\n1\tTownsfolk of Grimslade can be found in the town. You should speak to townsfolk of Grimslade.\t\n2\tReturn to Hildith\tHildith is in the Mead Hall of Grimslade. You should return to Hildith.\n",
})
